From 52457c32fb48c2987a55fa1eae8da5ef09ae7dfc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 19:33:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] docs(process): a contributor's claim must be live - stale
 after 48 h with nothing behind it

A contributor's claim comment used to stand for as long as the comment
existed, so claims whose agents had moved on days ago kept issues locked.
Maintainer, 2026-11-11: "unclaim those 8 old ones and let someone pick em
up and fix em they can't stall".

AGENTS.md "A claim comment is a claim": a contributor's claim is live
while there is an open PR for the issue, a commit on the claimant's
branch in the last 48 hours, or a comment by the claimant on the issue in
the last 48 hours. Otherwise it is stale: not mirrored, and a `claimed`
label behind it is removed with a comment. A claim also ends when the
claimant's last comment withdraws it or the maintainer releases it, and an
ended claim is never mirrored back from its old comment. The 4 h rule for
the owner account's own agents is unchanged.

review-prs step 4 (mirror and withdraw) follows the same rule.
PROCESS_VERSION 13 -> 14.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
