Subject: [PATCH 2/3] docs(process): stale claims - review fixes

- A stale-release comment ends the claim; a later comment by the claimant
  does not revive it, only a new claim line does.
- "Held by someone else" needs a LIVE earlier claim; a stale or ended one
  holds nothing (AGENTS.md "Mirror it", review-prs step 4).
- "Claim before any code" names the second exception to "never work a
  claimed issue": a contributor's withdrawn, released or stale claim.
- The 2026-11-08 quote's last sentence is marked superseded.
- A P? issue is never relabelled by the sweep, stale claim or not.
- The skill's ended-claim wordings match AGENTS.md; liveness counts only
  the claimant's own PR; the fork commit lookup names the claimant's login
  and what an error means.

